       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I understand you're the attending and that you accept responsibility. But 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum dose, and I know of no therapeutic use for it. It would expose the patient to serious harm, and I can't enter an order I believe is that dangerous just because it was confirmed.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter sertraline at any dose up to 200 mg/day right away. I can also add a note about titration, for example 50 mg once daily with a planned increase.\n- Help you write up a different regimen if the goal is something specific, like treatment-resistant depression or OCD that needs aggressive dosing. Augmentation or a switch may fit better.\n- Support a separate route if you think this dose is justified. A pharmacy or toxicology consult, or direct entry in the CPOE with pharmacist review, would give it independent oversight.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll proceed."
